{"step_index":1172,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:35:36Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:35:36+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:35:40+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:35:36+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:35:40+08:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\nquiz: active | autoRecordQuiz: { booleanValue: false } | subs: 1 [ 'asd/asd' ]\nquiz: template | autoRecordQuiz: undefined | subs: 0 []\n"}
{"step_index":1173,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:35:40Z","input_tokens":3966,"cache_read_tokens":122395,"output_tokens":2621,"thinking":"The evidence confirms the root cause: the `autoRecordQuiz` setting is disabled. This directly explains the observed behavior. Tracing the requested behavior reveals that all elements align perfectly with this setting.\n\n\nThe `index.html` logic unconditionally uploads quiz data regardless of the `autoRecordQuiz` setting. Specifically, the code executes the upload before checking the setting's value, resulting in uploads even when `autoRecordQuiz` is `false`. There's an inconsistency: the code treats missing or undefined `autoRecordQuiz` as `true`, while another part defaults it to `false` until changed. This indicates a potential bug due to this mismatch.\n\n\nThe updated code `const isAuto = st.autoRecordQuiz !== false;` appears to correctly control both the data upload and the user interface rendering based on the `autoRecordQuiz` setting. However, offline behavior introduces a complication: when offline, the `appendRecord` function may silently fail in downloaded HTML, but the new gate ensures no upload occurs when `autoRecordQuiz` is explicitly false, regardless of network status.\n\nFurther investigation of `teacher.html` is needed, specifically focusing on how the `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` value impacts the UI and data handling in the \"Options\" drawer before a save or quiz load and after an explicit `autoRecordQuiz: false` save. The analysis will check UI dependencies, save actions, and the loading of active quizzes.\n\n\n`teacher.html`'s initialization flow sets `autoRecordQuiz` to `false` initially, then attempts to load from `quizzes/active`. A key observation: `refreshSubmissions()` runs immediately on script load, potentially before `loadTeacherQuiz()` completes or when the setting is `false`. The submissions refresh's dependence on `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` or a saved value needs clarification, along with how `syncOptionsUI()` reacts to in-UI toggles of `autoRecordQuiz`.\n\n\nInitial concern centers on `quizzes/active/submissions` containing stale data despite `autoRecordQuiz` being off, as confirmed by \n<truncated 635 bytes>\ncordQuiz` and trigger `syncOptionsUI`, affecting both submission refresh and the UI display. Specifically, I'm checking the initial load: if auto-recording is set to false, it should prevent unnecessary network requests and immediately hide the UI controls, instead of loading then hiding. This also applies when the save button isn't yet clicked. I will look for race conditions during the initial page load before `loadTeacherQuiz()` is resolved, given the possibility of the data appearing, disappearing, and then reappearing.\n\n\nInitial analysis reveals an unnecessary network request from `refreshSubmissions()` on page load, even when the submissions view is hidden, due to the execution timing before quiz data loads. This results in either an unnecessary network call or a wasted round-trip if `autoRecordQuiz` is false. The optimal solution appears to be conditionally calling `refreshSubmissions()` only when the tab is visible and auto-recording is enabled, or after `loadTeacherQuiz()` completes, ensuring no premature execution or unneeded requests. The most elegant fix appears to be calling `syncOptionsUI()` from inside `populateQuizData()`.\n\n\nNo tests explicitly check initial `refreshSubmissions()`, though tests examined `tchEnv.els` and specific elements. The initial approach of calling `refreshSubmissions()` within `populateQuizData()` (or its `then()` block) addresses both immediate UI rendering and avoids unnecessary Firestore fetches when auto-recording is off. There is no need to actively delete data, as the UI modification will now hide the data whenever `autoRecordQuiz` is `false`.\n\n\nThe user turning Auto Record Quiz back ON presents a potential data display issue if they previously disabled it; the \"Clear Students\" button will reappear, but the old submission would still remain visible. Therefore, I need to ensure that enabling auto-recording doesn't show stale or cleared data. This requires investigating client-side best practices for data gating and user experience in conditional submission scenarios.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"730","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\scratch\\\\obf_tool\\\\tmp_backup\\\\teacher.html\"","StartLine":"655"}},{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"Firestore REST API stop unnecessary polling conditional feature toggle vanilla JS\""}},{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"web accessibility empty state notice hide action buttons unavailable feature vanilla HTML CSS\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
