{"step_index":1175,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:35:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:35:56+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:36:02+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:35:56+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:36:02+08:00\nThe search for \"Firestore REST API stop unnecessary polling conditional feature toggle vanilla JS\" returned the following summary:\nTo efficiently control, toggle, and completely halt unnecessary network requests or polling loops when using the **Firestore REST API** in vanilla JavaScript, you need a robust implementation pattern. \n\nBecause the raw Firestore REST API doesn't support persistent WebSockets/real-time streams out-of-the-box in standard browser environments (unlike the Firebase SDK's `onSnapshot`)[1], developers often rely on custom `setInterval` loops or recursive `setTimeout` pollers. If left unchecked, these can drain resources and rack up unnecessary database reads.\n\nThe following production-ready Vanilla JS solution implements:\n1. **A Conditional Feature Toggle** (to switch polling on/off dynamically).\n2. **AbortController Support** (to instantly cancel pending in-flight HTTP requests).\n3. **Visibility API Awareness** (automatically pauses polling when the user minimizes or switches tabs, preventing background waste).\n\n### Vanilla JavaScript Implementation\n\n```javascript\nclass FirestoreRestPoller {\n  constructor(config) {\n    this.projectId = config.projectId;\n    this.collection = config.collection;\n    this.apiKey = config.apiKey;\n    this.intervalMs = config.intervalMs || 10000; // Default: 10 seconds\n\n    this.timerId = null;\n    this.abortController = null;\n    \n    // 1. Conditional Feature Toggle State\n    this._isFeatureEnabled = config.initialState ?? true;\n\n    // Bind context\n    this.handleVisibilityChange = this.handleVisibilityChange.bind(this);\n    \n    // Initialize tab visibility listener to prevent background polling waste\n    document.addEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", this.handleVisibilityChange);\n    \n    // Evaluate initial state\n    this.evaluatePollingState();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Getter & Setter for the Feature Toggle\n   *\n<truncated 2663 bytes>\nhere if necessary\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Completely teardown listeners and polling (e.g., component unmount)\n   */\n  destroy() {\n    this.stop(\"Destroyed\");\n    document.removeEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", this.handleVisibilityChange);\n  }\n}\n\n// ==========================================\n// EXAMPLE USAGE:\n// ==========================================\n\nconst dbPoller = new FirestoreRestPoller({\n  projectId: \"your-firebase-project-id\",\n  collection: \"todos\",\n  apiKey: \"your-web-api-key\",\n  intervalMs: 15000, // Poll every 15 seconds\n  initialState: true // Feature toggle starts enabled\n});\n\n// Override data handler to update your Vanilla JS UI\ndbPoller.onData = (response) => {\n  const documents = response.documents || [];\n  document.getElementById(\"status\").innerText = `Loaded ${documents.length} docs at ${new Date().toLocaleTimeString()}`;\n};\n\n// --- Controlling via Feature Toggle UI ---\nconst toggleSwitch = document.getElementById(\"featureToggleCheckbox\");\n\ntoggleSwitch.addEventListener(\"change\", (event) => {\n  // Dynamically halts or resumes polling matching the feature flag state\n  dbPoller.isEnabled = event.target.checked;\n});\n```\n\n### Key Architectural Benefits:\n* **Zero Resource Leaks:** When `dbPoller.isEnabled = false` is triggered, it clears the JavaScript `setInterval` thread *and* invokes `abortController.abort()` to cancel network threads hanging on a database socket response.\n* **Visibility Optimization:** Browsers throttle background tabs differently. By listening to `visibilitychange`, the script proactively halts outbound REST requests when users navigate away, preventing wasted Firestore read billing quotas.\n\nSources:\n[1] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGcZfeP6l8A0SpTpZ3aBkExujf15ePuyl0yCA4VQ_-xrBA7bjB3R8aQ6tsJqdpDgoiE9w0FsPJu3Ea0cBcYqY-6DijRK1PJ0U6GaGe0Yjp5bC9moh3dNjIhW4Jg-FKUP8ddfQScGkUCnUe6owNo5WnwatVVo0WaxNF-LJ01SSrqeI4fn6a81eH6NxblDiLJl1M47ifDYQ==)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1176,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:35:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:35:56+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:36:07+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:35:56+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:36:07+08:00\nThe search for \"web accessibility empty state notice hide action buttons unavailable feature vanilla HTML CSS\" returned the following summary:\nWhen designing an **Empty State** notice that needs to completely hide action buttons due to an unavailable feature, relying strictly on visual CSS (`display: none`) is often enough for a simple removal. However, to build a truly accessible experience using vanilla HTML and CSS, you must ensure that state changes are handled cleanly so that screen readers and keyboard users aren't left with orphaned interactions or confusing layouts[1][2].\n\nHere is the best-practice approach using **Vanilla HTML and CSS**:\n\n### 1. The HTML Structure\nKeep the container semantic. If the entire action panel or button group needs to disappear conditionally based on feature availability, wrap it in a structural element or target the buttons directly. \n\n```html\n<section class=\"empty-state\" aria-labelledby=\"empty-title\">\n  <div class=\"empty-state__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">📁</div>\n  <h2 id=\"empty-title\" class=\"empty-state__title\">No Projects Found</h2>\n  <p class=\"empty-state__description\">You haven't created any projects yet. Get started by creating your first one.</p>\n  \n  <!-- Action button container -->\n  <div class=\"empty-state__actions\" id=\"action-buttons-group\">\n    <!-- Feature available: Button shows -->\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Create Project</button>\n    \n    <!-- Feature UNAVAILABLE: Handled via CSS or conditional rendering -->\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-secondary feature-unavailable\">Import from Template</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. The CSS Solution (Hiding Unavailable Features)\nIf a specific feature is permanently or temporarily unavailable and you want to **completely hide** its action button while keeping the empty state clean, use standard layout hiding[3][4]. \n\nUsing `\n<truncated 1828 bytes>\nnd pointer-events via CSS, though modern browsers universally support `inert`.*\n\n### Summary Checklist for Vanilla Implementation:\n1. **To completely remove the unavailable feature:** Use `display: none;` on the button or its wrapper. This natively resolves accessibility because hidden elements cannot be focused or read[3][4].\n2. **Never use `aria-hidden=\"true\"` alone on a button:** If you hide something with ARIA alone while leaving it focusable, it creates a severe \"keyboard trap\" where screen reader users can tab into an invisible, silent element[1]. Stick to `display: none` or `inert`[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [washington.edu](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF0Ks-6k-Slcr1HyqbzTTXxwJbmVFgRPyyerCR4nK04Hwi-1FzXEoz0rqDB_0bMwGjrN79m9ISj6ZtSzzYboGWn0vq0fcBGfxBuxlMmZB62s0ucqe7RgVYSa2_JVzX614ApBrYji16bKjoBxB-Ih9rJoEBi5oGNKIt2aAddLkV_)\n[2] [rocketvalidator.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEK4qB53FAaocINfCY0QOCBpui8g63wNzKooE6KVADRkf_nRCvTPX6Pb9ESi4HOFSZPXrqzpEZbVGvIOqdt4LR4RuBN8DUJYCB68F4iY-W0Aje4nsbOmV-5Zj6PtBkG5SfxGVwhbCJdxlpTjAzQ-5EOGyjlaw==)\n[3] [accessibleweb.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEduCrwGiFxO38xP1dHXJ0ufORR8suC_HA6CIBAokWSjKRnz0xosnZjo0dqwpbOBqcPkrEwaaLu4p-xyOibk2RqMT1DDnlcdEFyIhoS8dOFiwUZL1mOuq34TiGghOPH7_fXa9LqEdC4iGbjV5UxUpynJy05DYHULSjOlBFZ8DFxU4UE1-iiXBVU2cPLpSlvrLOiYshm0xFe)\n[4] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEyvqYii-hclboibhYMueeMN1FB-kUt56aQHOhQ5BmUo0DmJyuPCVnXoA9z_OUaR8aTmWO7dJTS2FqqYydMMHj6giTkD49-ZoC4ZYL17wGSBupiFbAL-DUTp3VxoRE0DHabJJZ7LW1AMeFFeQE9mW50WG2SU2dvMRPoBKha92eAc0T9jab0E1O1fZRv4VBtoZyH7aI1L5Aml4o7rkffY7CG)\n[5] [css-t