{"step_index":1177,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:36:07Z","input_tokens":7711,"cache_read_tokens":126362,"output_tokens":3173,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe quiz data handling unconditionally writes submission records, regardless of the auto-record setting, leading to unexpected behavior. The `finish()` and `showLock()` functions contain redundant logic for checking the auto-record state. A shared helper function, `isAutoRecord()`, will consolidate and clarify the auto-record logic across different parts of the code.\n\n\n`quizData.settings` might be undefined, leading to incorrect auto-record logic. The code incorrectly treats the absence of an auto-record setting as enabling recording. The `finish()` function should call `isAutoRecord()` to check before constructing submission data and performing remote writes, optimizing resource usage by skipping unnecessary operations when auto-record is off.\n\n\nExamining the HTML in `teacher.html` revealed several locations with auto-record logic including `#view-sub`. The logic for displaying completed students and managing submission counts requires inspection of several HTML lines to clarify auto-record gating and ensure correct behavior. Specifically, the rendering of `#view-sub` needs to be checked for potential auto-record conflicts.\n\n\nThe user's request involves displaying a notice on the submissions page and hiding the \"clear students\" button when auto-record is off. The notice will read \"Notice: This is only available to auto record quiz\". The clear students button is already hidden by default via `.hide`, so no change needed. Will confirm that logic within the `#view-sub` element operates as expected.\n\n\nExamining the CSS in `teacher.html` is essential to confirm that the `.hide` class correctly hides the \"clear students\" button, given potential specificity conflicts with `.row button`. The logic for hiding `#sub-count-badge` needs review; it should hide or reset to avoid stale counts when auto-record is disabled. The `#sub-actions` wrapper could be hidden to remove both the button and count, simplifying the hiding logic. The current callers and tests should be checked to un\n<truncated 323 bytes>\nte. Consolidating the `hide` class toggling for `#sub-desc`, `#sub-count-badge`, and `#clear-sub-btn` streamlines the implementation.\n\n\n`refreshSubmissions()` runs too early on boot, before the auto-record setting is known, and the polling interval unconditionally calls it. A new `syncSubmissionsAccess()` function should handle the conditional hiding of the button, badge, and description, displaying a notice, aborting any current requests, and stopping the polling timer when auto-record is off. This function will also gate `refreshSubmissions()` at its entry.\n\n\nThe existing logic doesn't prevent network requests when auto-record is off, even with conditional calls. Implementing a gating function ensures no requests are initiated when the feature is disabled, optimizing resource usage by preventing redundant network calls. Adding a visibility/tab-aware polling control eliminates timer callbacks and network fetches unless auto-record is on, the submissions tab is visible, and the document is not hidden. The `syncOptionsUI()` function called after toggling the auto-record setting requires further inspection for side effects.\n\n\nThe `syncOptionsUI()` function needs careful review; it should update the Submissions tab immediately after the auto-record setting is changed and also after the quiz data loads. This ensures consistent synchronization with the `Auto Record Quiz` setting, addressing all states and cases including after flipping the switch, without needing to save to the quiz. I need to consider a subtle edge case: What happens when the auto-record state is toggled on, but not yet saved?\n\n\nInitial observation: on load, the submissions tab UI correctly reflects the `autoRecordQuiz` state from Firestore. Enabling auto-record directly updates the UI, rendering the submissions tab immediately. The \"clear students\" button's conditional logic, including within the confirmation modal, seems sound with the `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` check. Now to check about the save button saving stale submissions in Firestore.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"65","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\scratch\\\\obf_tool\\\\tmp_backup\\\\teacher.html\"","StartLine":"1"}},{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"355","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\scratch\\\\obf_tool\\\\tmp_backup\\\\teacher.html\"","StartLine":"315"}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
